# Vesuva played as the first land of the game: there is no land on the battlefield for it to copy, so its "you may" asks
# nothing (CR 608.2d, 707.2: a copy of "any land on the battlefield" needs one there) and it enters untapped as itself
# (the ruling). The refusal `! Bot1.Accept` shows no question was put; the sibling scenario with a Forest out is asked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Vesuva
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Vesuva.Play
! Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Vesuva
Bot1.Battlefield.Vesuva.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Vesuva.Types = Land
